# Copy to .env.local. Everything is optional in development.
# `npm run setup` builds every engine locally; afterwards nothing depends on a third party.

# --- Where downloaded data and built engines live (keep it outside OneDrive/Dropbox) ---
# HEISYN_DATA_DIR=C:\heisyn-data

# --- Built-in engines (created by npm run setup) ---
# SEARCH_DB_PATH=C:\heisyn-data\search\search.db       # our own search index (search, reverse, nearby)
# PMTILES_PATH=C:\heisyn-data\tiles\region.pmtiles     # our own map tiles
# Map fonts are served from public/fonts (npm run data:fonts) unless GLYPHS_URL is set.

# --- Routing engine (npm run engine:routing, or the Valhalla container in infra/) ---
# VALHALLA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8002
# VROOM_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000                      # optional fleet optimiser (Docker)

# --- Our own servers (only if an engine runs on another machine we operate) ---
# HEISYN_OWN_HOSTS=routing.internal,10.0.0.5

# --- Optional alternatives ---
# PHOTON_URL=http://127.0.0.1:2322     # with SEARCH_ENGINE=photon, use a Photon server instead of the built-in index
# GLYPHS_URL=https://cdn.example.com/fonts/{fontstack}/{range}.pbf
# INDIA_BOUNDARY_GEOJSON=public/data/india-boundary.geojson
# DATA_GOV_IN_API_KEY=…                # PIN code import straight from data.gov.in

# --- Database (unset = SQLite at data/heisyn.db) ---
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://heisyn:change-me@127.0.0.1:5432/heisyn
# SQLITE_PATH=data/heisyn.db

# --- Secrets ---
# Used to derive the first-party map key. Generated into data/.secret if unset.
# HEISYN_SECRET=at-least-32-random-characters
# ADMIN_EMAILS=you@company.com
